-- title:
--   Character counting: #(G^∨/bG^∨)=#G[b] for finitely generated b
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring and $G$ an $A$-module (an additive commutative group with an $A$-module structure), and let $s \subseteq A$ be a subset. Assume $s$ is finite and that the $s$-torsion submodule $\mathrm{torsionBySet}\,A\,G\,s = \{x \in G : a \cdot x = 0 \text{ for all } a \in s\}$ is finite as a type. Write $G^\vee$ for `CharacterModule G`, the group of additive homomorphisms $G \to \mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Z}$, equipped with its $A$-module structure $(a \cdot \varphi)(x) = \varphi(a \cdot x)$, and let $\mathfrak{b} = \mathrm{Ideal.span}\,s$. The assertion is the equality of natural cardinalities
--   $$\#\bigl(G^\vee / (\mathfrak{b} \cdot \top)\bigr) \;=\; \#\,\mathrm{torsionBySet}\,A\,G\,s,$$
--   where $\mathfrak{b} \cdot \top$ is the submodule of $G^\vee$ generated by the products $a\varphi$ with $a \in \mathfrak{b}$ and $\varphi \in G^\vee$, and `Nat.card` is the cardinality of a finite type and $0$ otherwise (both sides are in fact finite under the hypotheses). No finiteness or Noetherian assumption is placed on $A$ or on $G$ beyond finiteness of $s$ and of the $s$-torsion.
--
--   This is the discrete shadow of Pontryagin duality for the exact sequence relating $\mathfrak{b}$-torsion and $\mathfrak{b}$-cotorsion: restriction of characters identifies $G^\vee/\mathfrak{b}G^\vee$ with the character group of $G[\mathfrak{b}]$. It supplies the cardinality bookkeeping used in the counting arguments [`Ideal.exists_natCard_torsionBySet_quotient_span_natCast_pow_le_natCard_quotient_pow_mul_pow_of_moduleFinite`](thm.html#Ideal.exists_natCard_torsionBySet_quotient_span_natCast_pow_le_natCard_quotient_pow_mul_pow_of_moduleFinite) and [`Submodule.natCard_torsionBySet_pow_linear_of_finite_torsionBy`](thm.html#Submodule.natCard_torsionBySet_pow_linear_of_finite_torsionBy).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CharacterModule_natCard_quotient_ideal_smul_top_eq_natCard_torsionBySet.lean

